{"title":"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lie on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f79a0be62330f80052b8447229914474e5e6903.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AFE=\\angle BDF=\\angle CED.\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"13\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d8aa423de2031c09aa06a1687767414dbb8120d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0af44578003bbd64382d00ed07ed2e33099284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2b7d9af12c551508264ff8ed054503c4e1b890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> be the circumcenters of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378fc67ebfe29ddad36d7bab7b5851c10738c166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFE$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b93a2dc17d4cf5e91cf1edaa02b2a16f690e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5309b25510f426ca00c957623bd0396c79e4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CED$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumcenters of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9e8b2c23e0545ef6de81f0ea578173e9ab7a64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DEF$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/5/b05c844d6d1a5d916d2a6a78d3a38ea13c28d1b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_AO_BO_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />, respectively. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00c790407cf1ea6e6b8dda1272b335c932ae1dea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM=ON$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c577fac50af6fafc3d126ec1ee20c9be416346fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(13cm); import geometry;  pair A = (3.5,4); pair B = (0, 0); pair C = (5, 0); pair D = (2.833019214522, 0); pair E = (4.4980821730446, 1.3384475385477); pair F = (2.0594882641949, 2.3537008733656); pair M = circumcenter(A,B,C); pair N = circumcenter(D,E,F); pair O_A = circumcenter(A,F,E); pair O_B = circumcenter(B,D,F); pair O_C = circumcenter(C,E,D); pair O = circumcenter(O_A,O_B,O_C); pair P = (3.0430813826498, 1.0908780166291); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(D--E--F--cycle); draw(O_A--O_B--O_C--cycle); draw(A--P); draw(B--P); draw(C--P); draw(D--P); draw(E--P); draw(F--P); draw(M--P); draw(N--P); draw(O--P); draw(O_A--P); draw(O_B--P); draw(O_C--P); draw(circumcircle(A,E,F), lightblue); draw(circumcircle(B,D,F), lightblue); draw(circumcircle(C,E,D), lightblue); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, dir(105)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, dir(255)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, dir(0)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;, D, dir(270)); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;, E, dir(45)); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, dir(135)); dot(&quot;$O_A$&quot;, O_A, dir(45)); dot(&quot;$O_B$&quot;, O_B, dir(135)); dot(&quot;$O_C$&quot;, O_C, dir(315)); dot(&quot;$P$&quot;, P, 2*dir(225)); dot(&quot;$M$&quot;, M, dir(45)); dot(&quot;$N$&quot;, N, dir(45)); dot(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, dir(45)); markangle(n=1, p=red, radius=12.0, E,F,A); markangle(n=1, p=red, radius=12.0, E,P,A); markangle(n=1, p=red, radius=12.0, D,E,C); markangle(n=1, p=red, radius=12.0, D,P,C); markangle(n=1, p=red, radius=12.0, F,D,B); markangle(n=1, p=red, radius=12.0, F,P,B); markangle(n=1, p=orange, radius=18.0, O_A,P,A); markangle(n=1, p=orange, radius=18.0, O_B,P,B); markangle(n=1, p=orange, radius=18.0, O_C,P,C); markangle(n=1, p=orange, radius=18.0, O,P,M); markangle(n=1, p=red, radius=8.0, N,P,M); [/asy]\" width=\"615\" height=\"565\" />\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where the circumcircles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608bb82ba507ff58202e9189f262289737cd92e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AFE}, \\triangle{BDF}, \\triangle{CED}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"198\" height=\"18\" /> intersect, which we know exists because it is the Miquel point of the given configuration.\n</p><p><b>Claim 1:</b> We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/a/12a570bc373597f56e1d1c39b77804e2688bd286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC} \\sim \\triangle{EFD} \\sim \\triangle{O_AO_BO_C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"261\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Proof:</b> For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/6527e754a66edce640cbebf3707f93e8caec18e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC} \\sim \\triangle{O_AO_BO_C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"18\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/d/bfd5eb71f1008e47faf2b1928bea77be14f7d39a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CAB} = \\angle{EAP} + \\angle{PAF} = \\angle{O_CO_AP} + \\angle{PO_AO_B} = \\angle{O_CO_AO_B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"526\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a7f98f661665c510749d45814aab08bd20a9fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BCA} = \\angle{DCP} + \\angle{PCE} = \\angle{O_BO_CP} + \\angle{PO_CO_A} = \\angle{O_BO_CO_A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"529\" height=\"17\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/8/4d8aa423de2031c09aa06a1687767414dbb8120d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"23\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0af44578003bbd64382d00ed07ed2e33099284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2b7d9af12c551508264ff8ed054503c4e1b890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> being the centers of circumcircles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608bb82ba507ff58202e9189f262289737cd92e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AFE}, \\triangle{BDF}, \\triangle{CED}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"198\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5eaa3ba6f02e70ddfe6bd646bebb4246fcac286.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC} \\sim \\triangle{EFD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />, we have from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a438b572cff3a7bde979bfe4dcdeb58bfd96c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AFE} = \\angle{BDF} = \\angle{CED}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"220\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/8/c18e240b7c7dbc4b2e6da70cd13ba155dc475c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D, E, F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" /> lying on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/e/d8efab0f68cfe83cd75f01f951920f544da89d49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC, CA, AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" /> respectively that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/1323a651f81083ba64a835b4fc6bf5dd6edeaec7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[180^\\circ = \\angle{CED} + \\angle{DEF} + \\angle{FEA} = \\angle{AFE} + \\angle{CAB} + \\angle{FEA} \\implies \\angle{DEF} = \\angle{CAB}\\]\" width=\"659\" height=\"14\" /> and analogously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6798fe9ec2930b191d44544696d22baa58381f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FDE} = \\angle{BCA}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><b>Claim 2:</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the spiral similarities <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/740cbb392d797e2ac22e54516cc0f5bc9ab256ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{1}, s_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> sending <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1466d39d58bc05988b392a3896a87c06cb8ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EFD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/54544810c8e4ba73f0ada9b2628ef3a9532bf47e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle O_AO_BO_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> respectively.\n</p><p><b>Proof:</b> For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f30c7e3b6cdb6b71f1120ed9f58573990e1a273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> note by cyclic quadrilaterals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/7/8f7d7bcf87f2eb74e35d470aeca1b01c0eee8c67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEPF, CDPE, BFPD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" /> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e06fe49c9ad1e03bb324e5836c99ca49a4b404.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle AFE = \\angle BDF = \\angle CED = \\angle CPD = \\angle BPF = \\angle EPA,\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"16\" /> which we call <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be204d54bf33d321cbb17451336850d7fe577787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEP = \\angle BFP = \\angle CDP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"218\" height=\"14\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def28f2e5b6cc32272b6710040695adabd4487f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AEP \\sim \\triangle BFP \\sim \\triangle CDP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f30c7e3b6cdb6b71f1120ed9f58573990e1a273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> rotates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and scales down by the common ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d8cbaf61a624c236133ca7a0bb4ef296069e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AP}{PE} = \\frac{BP}{PF} = \\frac{CP}{PD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"150\" height=\"39\" /> to precisely yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1466d39d58bc05988b392a3896a87c06cb8ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EFD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42bb0ecde26e26473f41293b509c7989047aa3b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> note that from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe7f6e7b178b226eb3451383f6fed244951d4cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PDC = \\angle PEA = \\angle PFB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"218\" height=\"14\" /> follows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace25e34a464d513707941c28e08aab104800890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle APO_A = \\angle BPO_B = \\angle CPO_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"249\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/b/37b1a9ccc7e2ecf2381d9972546f4708dff248dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PO_AA = \\angle PO_BB = \\angle PO_CC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"249\" height=\"17\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502ee733d59e8b7ac6c2fb8ea7eb8bc2eaeefdfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle APO_A \\sim \\triangle BPO_B \\sim \\triangle CPO_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"259\" height=\"18\" /> and similarly suffices to imply that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42bb0ecde26e26473f41293b509c7989047aa3b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>To finish, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/171ab7df26ee39fd29419037f3b6784b3ef8bc3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{1}(M) = N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/d/87dab088bb6e6b14e30bd9cd03b846194280b00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{2}(M) = O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fa98e442666dd70795c777dbb835a659c653972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{1}(A) = E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/8/5b8008cdd12626c601e0cb3a9d87caf3b8a9cb58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{2}(A) = O_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" /> while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/740cbb392d797e2ac22e54516cc0f5bc9ab256ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_{1}, s_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> share the same center, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/4/bb42c9da70b60fcc9269fbc2d3d4008c36126e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle MON \\sim \\triangle AO_AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804b73d392f6dd561b212c9c58cc1844a55c3b31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM = ON$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26c64b79b4dbd4cb023dbf329c0ea7d6cef2609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_AA = O_AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>~hnkevin42\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO\" title=\"2026 USAMO\">2026 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018033424\nCache expiry: 86